// src/v4/std/primitive.dag
//
// Scope: target-grounded primitives with declared algebra inhabitance.
// Anchor: Per-target — Rust Reference §Types, Python Data Model, Go Spec (per THESIS:173)
//
// Owns:
//   - Int, Float, String, Char, Bool
//   - inhabitance: Int -> OrderedRing, String -> FreeMonoid<Char>, etc.
//   - target-side mapping is structural homomorphism, not name-keyed table
//   - Hash — opaque fixed-width digest (B1, operator-ratified 2026-05-15).
//     Equality only; NO content accessor (same opacity discipline as the
//     K-1 `Symbol`). This is the content-address carrier. The fold that
//     produces it — `content_hash : Node -> Hash`, a Merkle catamorphism
//     over the A1-canonical Node — is declared in `std/node.dag` (the T-1
//     worker encodes it per relay; it belongs with the canonical-form
//     clause). ONE scheme, consumed by T-15 (fixed point) / T-20 (pin) /
//     T-21 (unchanged-subgraph) / the A3 reproduction check / C5
//     RoundTrips. Not workflow-level — workflow consumes it; substrate
//     defines identity.
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag: Atom
//   - std/algebra.dag: OrderedRing, FreeMonoid
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-3
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.std.primitive

